    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_15",
      "quote": "We included studies that compared covid-19 rates, clinical manifestations... between pregnant and recently pregnant and non-pregnant women of reproductive age, and those that compared maternal and perinatal outcomes in pregnant women with and without covid-19. In studies comparing maternal and perinatal outcomes of pregnant women with covid-19 to those without, we classified the comparative controls as being historical if the cohort of pregnant women without covid-19 gave birth before December 2019.",
      "reason": "Synthesis groups (comparative vs non-comparative cohorts; pregnant vs non-pregnant; covid-19 vs no covid-19; historical vs concurrent controls) are specified and linked to the review comparisons, with further subgroup groupings in text_16."
